00:14:36,910 --> 00:14:40,570
Let's say you start to brainstorm a list of all the emotions you've ever

133
00:14:40,570 --> 00:14:43,570
experienced. Just for fun, try it now.

134
00:14:44,470 --> 00:14:45,510
What's on your list?

135
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:50,630
Chances are you included things like happy, sad, excited,

136
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:59,820
angry, afraid, grateful, proud, scared, confused, stressed, relaxed and amazed.

137
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:06,990
Now sort your list into two categories, positive emotions and negative emotions.

138
00:15:08,010 --> 00:15:13,290
Feeling both positive and negative emotions is a natural part of being human.

139
00:15:13,290 --> 00:15:19,210
We might use the word negative to describe more difficult emotions, but it doesn't

140
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:22,490
mean those emotions are bad or we shouldn't have them.

141
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:28,490
Still, most people would probably rather feel a positive emotion than a negative

142
00:15:28,490 --> 00:15:34,890
one. It's likely you'd prefer to feel happy instead of sad or confident instead of

143
00:15:34,890 --> 00:15:39,390
insecure. What matters is how our emotions are balanced,

144
00:15:40,170 --> 00:15:44,450
how much of each type of emotion, positive or negative, we experience.

145
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:51,810
Negative emotions warn us of threats or challenges that we may need to deal with.

146
00:15:52,150 --> 00:15:55,450
For example, fear can alert us to possible danger.

147
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:59,170
It's a signal that we might need to protect ourselves.

148
00:15:59,870 --> 00:16:05,330
Angry feelings warn us that someone is stepping on our toes, crossing a boundary or

149
00:16:05,330 --> 00:16:06,850
violating our trust.

150
00:16:07,830 --> 00:16:11,450
Anger can be a signal that we might need to act on our own behalf.

151
00:16:13,170 --> 00:16:15,090
emotions focus our awareness.

152
00:16:16,070 --> 00:16:20,210
They help us to zero in on a problem so we can deal with it.

153
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:26,430
But too many negative emotions can make us feel overwhelmed, anxious, exhausted or

154
00:16:26,430 --> 00:16:33,110
stressed out. When negative emotions are out of balance, problems might seem too big

155
00:16:33,110 --> 00:16:39,330
to handle. The more we dwell on negative emotions, the more negative we begin to

156
00:16:40,470 --> 00:16:43,070
Focusing on negativity just keeps it going.

157
00:16:44,550 --> 00:16:49,630
Positive emotions balance out negative ones, but they have other powerful benefits

158
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:57,330
too. Instead of narrowing our focus, negative emotions do, positive emotions affect

159
00:16:57,330 --> 00:17:02,270
our brains in ways that increase our awareness, attention and memory.

160
00:17:03,370 --> 00:17:05,550
They help us take in more information,

161
00:17:06,210 --> 00:17:12,050
hold several ideas in mind at once, and understand how different ideas relate to

162
00:17:12,050 --> 00:17:18,890
each other. When positive emotions open us up to new possibilities, we are more able

163
00:17:18,890 --> 00:17:20,850
to learn and build on our skills.

164
00:17:21,990 --> 00:17:24,830
That leads to doing better on tasks and tests.

165
00:17:26,450 --> 00:17:31,330
People who have plenty of positive emotions in their everyday lives, tend to be

166
00:17:31,330 --> 00:17:35,870
happier, healthier, learn better, and get along well with others.

